  "summary": "Generic runtime object layer. UI components are constructed through a shared pattern (base init, vtable install at +0x0, per-component data-source pointer at +0x31C, state words at +0x324..0x330, component ID at +0x334, text-handle linked-list registration, optional post-init action-ID dispatch). A second constructor family initializes through sub_48C070 and writes a literal id at +0x31C plus a bound global pointer at +0x320. Screen setup methods bind a mode global and a list pointer into +0x320/+0x324 and commit formatted text to the UI edit buffer. Several functions verify names through the dword_7CD8C0 dispatch interface (vtable slot +28, object types 11/12/13/19/3). Scene/season name lists are walked to resolve the current scene and trigger its loader. A destructor frees owned buffers and paired allocations, and a parser rebuilds a coordinate linked list from a .rt track file. All structure is DERIVED/GUESS; common ownership of the +0x320/+0x324 pattern is not proven across members.",
